.TH LYFY 1 "2026-10-29" "lyfy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lyfy \- declarative system maintenance for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B lint
.RB [ \-\-elevate [=auto|never|required]]
.br
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B save
.br
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.RB [ \-\-write ]
.br
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B fmt
.RB [ \-\-write ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lyfy
inspects an Arch Linux system, records concrete host configuration and plans
reconciliation with saved state.
The supported release architecture is x86_64.
.PP
There are exactly four commands:
.BR lint ,
.BR fmt ,
.BR save
and
.BR apply .
Global options may appear before or after the command.
Each setting has a snake_case option and a corresponding
.B LYFY_UPPER_CASE
environment variable.
Precedence is option, environment, TOML configuration, then default.
See
.BR lyfy.conf (5)
for settings, scope defaults and configuration lookup.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lint
Inspect the Arch policy without changing the managed system.
Checks include pending pacnew/pacsave files, pacman database consistency,
missing package files, package metadata drift, files without a package owner,
orphan dependencies, running kernel state, the configured UKI policy and
failed systemd units.
Incomplete and skipped checks are reported explicitly.
Read-only package operations use dynamically linked libalpm directly.
File checks compare package mtree metadata and stream SHA-256 reads.
JSON package findings include typed evidence for changed fields.
Terminals show updating stage spinners and package-count bars on stderr.
Redirected stderr uses plain stage messages and package counts.
The final human report explains rule categories, findings and remedies.
JSON, TOML, YAML, Markdown and SARIF 2.1.0 are also available.
Report data goes to stdout unless output_file selects a new private file.
The CLI owns all rendering and report formats.
.IP
Interactive scans of the running system request sudo automatically for a
non-root user when stdin and stderr are terminals.
This is the default
.B \-\-elevate=auto
policy.
.B \-\-elevate=never
keeps existing privileges.
Bare
.B \-\-elevate
or
.B \-\-elevate=required
requests sudo even for noninteractive launches or alternative roots.
The child runs only read-only lint, preserving the original resolved user
settings and HOME/XDG-derived paths rather than choosing root's defaults.
It explicitly disables further elevation.
When scanning without sudo, inaccessible paths are aggregated per check as
coverage diagnostics and accessible checks continue.
Partial coverage returns exit status 2.
The elevated worker returns report data to the original process, which renders
and saves it as the original invoking user.
Root access does not bypass every access policy or missing mount.
.IP
UKI is a lyfy policy, not an Arch Linux requirement.
Unowned files, orphan packages and modified package metadata require review.
.TP
.B save
Capture files, Unix permissions including special bits, ownership, symlinks,
hardlinks, file/directory ACLs/xattr and optional package inventory.
Files edited in place are saved directly, without templates.
.IP
.B \-\-dry_run
previews changes without publishing snapshots, initializing storage or writing
exports. Reports compare against the previous effective state. Unchanged saves
reuse their snapshot in both Git and directory storage. Progress uses stderr.
.IP
Named VFS mounts route arbitrary nested paths to Git, directory or S3.
The longest component-prefix match owns a path, including unselected children.
History/current-only policy, pinned-base retention, replicas and age encryption
are configured per mount/backend. Explicit selected_mounts controls data restore.
export_file writes a complete committed archive; import_file supplies verified
state for save or apply. Select exactly one scope for export/import.
.IP
Git is the default storage format.
The repository contains ordinary payload files and JSON metadata under
.IR hosts/host/ .
Saving commits the host state locally on the current attached branch and
creates no empty commit for unchanged state.
Existing repository changes must be committed, stashed or resolved first.
Saving never implicitly pushes or merges.
.IP
.B \-\-base_host
selects an optional common base when saving.
The resulting host overlay pins that base to an immutable revision.
Saving common later does not rewrite already saved host overlays.
.TP
.B apply
Plan reconciliation with the selected host and snapshot.
The plan compares desired content, live content and the last applied receipt
for the same host, root and home directory.
A different existing target on first deployment is a conflict.
.IP
.B \-\-write
executes a conflict-free plan, backing up file preimages and recording a
private transaction journal before target writes.
.B \-\-overwrite true
permits reviewed conflicting replacements.
Tracked deletions additionally require
.BR "\-\-prune true" .
Untracked files are retained, and directory deletion is nonrecursive.
.IP
Package restoration additionally requires
.BR "\-\-install_packages true" ,
existing root privileges and text display.
It uses a full pacman upgrade for missing native packages and restores
affected installation reasons.
Missing foreign packages require deliberate handling.
Extra packages are not removed and recorded versions are not forced.
.TP
.B fmt
Plan supported deterministic policy fixes.
.B \-\-write
executes them through the same backup and journal mechanism as apply.
Currently only pacnew files identical to their active configuration are
removed automatically.
Other findings require manual review.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-elevate [=auto|never|required]
Choose the sudo policy for lint or save.
The default auto policy requests authentication only when stdin and stderr
are terminals and root is /.
Never disables the request; required always requests it for a non-root user.
An omitted value means required. A value must follow an equals sign.
Sudo must be installed and authorize the operation; it owns the password prompt.
Refusal or failure stops that launch.
This launch policy has no configuration key or environment equivalent.
For save, only protected capture runs elevated. The original caller validates
a private channel and publishes using their own storage credentials.
.TP
.B \-\-dry_run
Preview save without repository/state/remote/export writes.
The alias \-\-dry-run is also accepted.
If already root, lint runs directly.
.TP
.BI \-\-config_file " path"
Use this required TOML file instead of XDG configuration lookup.
The environment equivalent is
.BR LYFY_CONFIG_FILE .
This selector cannot be specified inside the configuration file itself.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " text|json|toml|yaml|markdown|sarif"
Select report format. Markdown and SARIF are lint-only.
Interactive package execution requires text display.
.TP
.BI \-\-output_file " path"
Save a lint report to a new private file with mode 0600.
The parent directory must exist. Publication is atomic and never replaces an
existing file, directory or symlink. A value of - selects stdout.
With a file destination stdout is empty; stderr confirms the saved report.
.TP
.BI \-\-progress " auto|plain|never"
Select lint progress, default auto.
Auto uses an updating display for terminal stderr unless TERM is unset or dumb;
otherwise it uses plain messages. Never hides scan feedback.
NO_COLOR disables colors. Progress never enters the report.
.TP
.BI \-\-disabled_rules " rule,rule"
Replace the list of excluded rule IDs. Unknown IDs are errors.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail_on " info|warning|error"
Set the minimum finding severity that fails a complete scan.
The default is warning. Lower-severity findings remain visible.
.TP
.B \-\-write
Grant execution permission for apply or fmt.
This permission has no configuration key or environment equivalent.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show the executable version.
.PP
All configuration settings documented in
.BR lyfy.conf (5)
also accept the corresponding
.B \-\-snake_case
global option.
Booleans require an explicit true or false value.
Comma-separated list overrides replace the lower-priority list.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
lyfy lint
lyfy lint \-\-elevate=never
lyfy lint \-\-elevate
lyfy lint \-\-format sarif \-\-output_file laptop.sarif
lyfy lint \-\-format json \-\-progress never
lyfy save \-\-host common
lyfy save \-\-host laptop \-\-base_host common
lyfy apply \-\-host laptop
lyfy apply \-\-host laptop \-\-write
lyfy fmt
.fi
.PP
Review the plan before selecting overwrite, prune or package restoration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lyfy/config.toml
User configuration, defaulting to
.IR ~/.config/lyfy/config.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/lyfy/config.toml
System configuration locations searched after the user's file.
The default directory is
.IR /etc/xdg .
The first readable configuration file wins as a whole.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/lyfy
Default state repository, falling back to
.IR ~/.local/share/lyfy .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/lyfy
Receipts, locks and transaction journals, falling back to
.IR ~/.local/state/lyfy .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation succeeded.
An apply preview with planned changes and no conflicts succeeds.
.TP
.B 1
A complete scan has outstanding findings at or above fail_on, or conflicts
or pending fmt fixes remain.
.TP
.B 2
Coverage is incomplete, or an operational, configuration or report export
error prevented completion.
.SH LIMITATIONS
External tool queries have a 120-second time limit.
Timeouts remain explicit incomplete checks.
Native package checks stream file contents with bounded memory and report
package progress; full SHA-256 inspection can take several minutes.
UID/GID checks in a user namespace with shifted or incomplete identity mappings
are reported as incomplete rather than as changed system ownership.
.PP
Individual file replacements are atomic; a multi-file operation is not one
atomic filesystem transaction.
Failures leave original file objects and a recovery journal in
.IR state_dir/transactions/ .
Automatic rollback, crash resume, AUR builds and boot migration are not
implemented.
.PP
Capture reports unsupported sockets/devices, symlink attributes and non-UTF-8
names. Strict capture blocks publication on any error. Explicit capture_errors
skip records incomplete state and returns 2; apply refuses incomplete snapshots.
Symbolic links are recorded without following their targets.
Active identity/credential files are always excluded from capture.
Target writes refuse symlink parents.
Stop concurrent edits and package transactions while capturing or applying
state; lyfy does not freeze the filesystem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lyfy.conf (5),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR bootctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR git (1)
